  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">As per the priorities identified in cooperation with the General Directorate of Fire Protection and Rescue Service, the key indicators include:
- # of municipal firefighting stations constructed / reconstructed
- # of heavy firefighting equipment provided
- # of firefighter PPEs provided
- # of training curricula developed
- # of trainings delivered
- # of firefighters participating in trainings, from target/beneficiary municipalities
- # of firefighters obtaining training certifications, from target/beneficiary municipalities</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- A major and persisting problem for the municipal firefighter teams is the lack of structured physical and content-wise training system for employees, especially for the newly municipal recruits. 
- The completion of municipal stations, especially for municipalities being county/prefectural centres, with rescue/rapid intervention vehicles, is another necessity, as is countering the lack of firefighting equipment at stations.
- Then the overall state of physical infrastructure and equipment is poor and not affordable to most municipalities hosting the decentralized service.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Technical design and finalization of BoQ completed for 3 municipal firefighting stations
- Works for the construction of 3 municipal firefighting stations started and in at least 2, completed
- Procurement of 3 containers with rescue equipment launched 
- Procurement of 3 fire extinguishers trucks launched
- Procurement of 156 Firefighter PPEs completed
- 3 training curricula developed
- 6 trainings delivered</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">-Documents for RFP procedure for selection of design &amp; supervision company for construction of 3 municipal firefighting stations completed and ready to be announced. 
- Procurement of 3 USAR containers with rescue equipment in the last phase of finalization. 
- Procurement of 3 fire extinguishers trucks launched and cancelled due to lack of value for money by the received bidders. 
- Procurement of 169 Firefighter PPEs completed, contract signed.
- training curricula developed in the process of development in collaboration with the GD of AFPRS
- 6 trainings delivered</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
